{"article_ids": ["44bd775b8ffe162a"], "canonical_title": "Amazon says hackers' AI agents found and exploited 0-day with little human input", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.8, "description": "Amazon reported that attackers employed AI agents, using the Cairn AI framework, to automatically locate and exploit a previously unknown (0‑day) software vulnerability, requiring little direct human involvement. The same Cairn framework is noted as being useful for both defenders and attackers.", "entities": ["org:amazon"], "first_seen": "2026-11-24T12:30:05Z", "id": "evt_44bd775b8ffe162a", "importance_score": 6.543, "last_updated": "2026-11-24T12:30:05Z", "source_ids": ["ars-technica"]}
{"article_ids": ["5b5230fa758613ad"], "canonical_title": "RECAP: Training Long-horizon LLM Agents with Context Compaction", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "The paper titled RECAP proposes a reinforcement‑learning framework that trains large language model (LLM) agents to compress their interaction histories into summarized representations while simultaneously learning the agent policy. This joint training addresses the difficulty of preserving task‑relevant information in the summaries, which affect success over many future steps, enabling agents to operate under strict context‑size limits for long‑horizon tasks.", "entities": ["term:reca", "term:recap"], "first_seen": "2026-11-25T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_5b5230fa758613ad", "importance_score": 6.34, "last_updated": "2026-11-25T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-cl"]}
{"article_ids": ["5e8eba5b15ac6044"], "canonical_title": "Three LLM inflection points in twelve months", "category": "model_release", "confidence": 0.4, "description": "Simon Willison delivered a keynote at the AI Engineer Code Summit, outlining three significant inflection points in large language model (LLM) capabilities over the past twelve months, with a focus on coding agents. He noted that November 24, 2026 marks the one‑year anniversary of the release of Claude Opus 4.5.", "entities": [], "first_seen": "2026-11-24T23:02:07Z", "id": "evt_5e8eba5b15ac6044", "importance_score": 6.138, "last_updated": "2026-11-24T23:02:07Z", "source_ids": ["simon-willison"]}
{"article_ids": ["b77f0e482deef83a"], "canonical_title": "SpatialCraft: Evolving Procedural Intelligence from Experience and Skills for Spatial Reasoning Agents", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.7, "description": "The arXiv preprint SpatialCraft introduces a method for spatial reasoning agents to evolve procedural intelligence from experience and skill representations, aiming to improve how agents select, order, and interpret outputs from external 3D reconstruction, segmentation, and geometric computation tools, addressing the bottleneck of tool orchestration in stateless agents.", "entities": ["term:mllm"], "first_seen": "2026-11-25T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_b77f0e482deef83a", "importance_score": 5.94, "last_updated": "2026-11-25T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["ac2f786b30f6d457", "e9888a1f843c90b6"], "canonical_title": "GPT-6 models demonstrate intrinsic protein-design capabilities", "category": "other", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "OpenAI reports that GPT‑6 models can design protein structures and sequences, using reasoning and code, and laboratory tests showed binding evidence on five targets. Separately, an arXiv pre‑print notes that frontier models such as GPT‑6 Astra perform substantial reasoning without a legible chain‑of‑thought, making real‑time monitoring costly, and proposes a monitorable‑by‑design architectural modification for future LLMs.", "entities": ["model:gpt", "model:gpt-6", "term:gpt"], "first_seen": "2026-11-24T13:00:00Z", "id": "evt_ac2f786b30f6d457", "importance_score": 5.77, "last_updated": "2026-11-25T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["openai", "arxiv-cs-ai"]}
